---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const email = '[SUPPORT EMAIL]';

const short = [
  { title: 'No accounts', text: 'Nobody signs up or logs in.' },
  { title: 'No personal data', text: "We don't collect names, photos, locations or contacts." },
  { title: 'No tracking', text: 'No analytics or tracking tools follow your child around.' },
  { title: 'Stays on the device', text: 'Game progress and settings live only on your iPhone or iPad.' },
];
---

<Base page="privacy" title="Where's My Crown? – Privacy Policy" description="How Where's My Crown? handles your family's information.">
  <section class="night">
    <div class="container narrow hero">
      <h1 class="title">PRIVACY POLICY</h1>
      <p>Effective date: [DATE]</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Remove this banner once the policy has been reviewed. -->
  <div class="container narrow draft-wrap">
    <p role="note" class="draft">
      <strong>Draft:</strong> this policy describes how the app is designed to work. Fill in the bracketed details
      and have it reviewed by someone qualified before publishing; children's apps have extra legal requirements
      (such as COPPA in the US and GDPR in the EU and UK).
    </p>
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="short-h">
    <div class="container narrow short">
      <h2 id="short-h" class="pixel">The short version</h2>
      <div class="cards">
        {short.map((s) => (
          <div class="card">
            <p class="ui">{s.title}</p>
            <p>{s.text}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="container narrow policy">
    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Where's My Crown? ("the app") is made by [LEGAL NAME OF DEVELOPER], trading as Nutrx Labs ("we", "us"). You
        can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> or [POSTAL ADDRESS].
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">What the app keeps on your device</h2>
      <p>To work, the app saves a few things on the device itself. They are never sent to us:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>which mazes are unlocked;</li>
        <li>settings such as sound and read-aloud on or off;</li>
        <li>dress-up choices (dress and hair colours, and whether the little sister comes along);</li>
        <li>whether the Royal Pass has been bought.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Deleting the app deletes this information.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        The Royal Pass is bought through Apple's App Store. Apple handles the payment; we never see your name,
        payment card or Apple Account details. Apple tells the app only whether the purchase was made, so it can
        unlock the helpers. Purchases sit behind a grown-up question so children can't buy by accident.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">Advertising</h2>
      <p class="choose">[CHOOSE ONE BEFORE PUBLISHING]</p>
      <p>
        <strong>If the app shows ads:</strong> in the free version, a short ad plays only when a player chooses to
        bring a helper. Ads are provided by [AD NETWORK NAME], which is certified for apps used by children. Ads are
        contextual only: they are not based on your child's behaviour, and no advertising identifier or personal
        information is used to target them. [AD NETWORK NAME]'s own privacy policy is at [LINK]. Buying the Royal
        Pass removes ads completely.
      </p>
      <p><strong>If the app has no ads:</strong> the app contains no advertising of any kind.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">Read aloud</h2>
      <p>
        The voice that reads messages aloud is [built into the app as recorded audio / produced by your device's own
        speech feature]. Nothing your child does is recorded, and the app does not use the microphone or camera.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The app is made for young children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children, and the
        app has no chat, sharing or social features. If you believe a child has sent us personal information (for
        example by email), contact us and we will delete it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">If you email us</h2>
      <p>
        If you write to us for support, we use your email address and message only to answer you. We keep support
        emails for [PERIOD] and then delete them. You can ask us to delete them sooner at any time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">This website</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not use cookies or analytics. [UPDATE IF THAT CHANGES, OR NAME YOUR HOSTING PROVIDER IF IT
        KEEPS SERVER LOGS.]
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights to ask what information we hold about you, to correct it or
        to have it deleted. Because the app doesn't collect personal information, the only information we might hold
        is a support email you sent us. Write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> and we'll help.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we change how the app handles information, we'll update this page and the effective date at the top before
        the change takes effect. If a change would mean collecting any personal information from children, we would
        ask for a parent's permission first, as the law requires.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p>Questions? See <a href="/support">Support</a> or email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-top: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 64px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(22px, 3.6vw, 36px); line-height: 1.35; }
  .hero p { font-size: 18px; color: var(--on-night-2); }

  .draft-wrap { padding-top: 40px; }
  .draft {
    padding: 16px 20px;
    background: #FFE3EF;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px #B8407A;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: #5A1F3A;
  }

  .short {
    padding-top: 40px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .short h2 { font-size: clamp(16px, 2.2vw, 22px); line-height: 1.5; }
  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(240px, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .card {
    background: var(--card);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--ink);
    padding: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .card .ui { font-size: 22px; line-height: normal; }

  .policy {
    padding-top: 48px;
    padding-bottom: 80px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 36px;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .policy section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .policy h2 { font-size: 28px; }
  .policy ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 24px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .choose {
    padding: 12px 16px;
    background: #FFF1C9;
    box-shadow: inset 4px 0 0 var(--gold-deep);
  }
</style>
